      "description": "Watch Sarmiento Junin vs Huracan highlights and goals from Argentine Primera División on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 16, 2026. The clash between Sarmiento Junin and Huracan brought high-stakes energy to the pitch as both sides vied for control in a hard-fought encounter. Played on August 16, 2026, in the Liga Profesional Argentina , the match was defined by tactical battles and significant momentum shifts. Opening momentum The game started with an aggressive pace, with Sarmiento Junin finding their breakthrough in the 30th minute courtesy of a strike from Junior Marabel . The first half remained physical, with referees busy noting down names as Rodrigo Fernandez and Julian Mavilla both found themselves in the book before the half-time whistle. Second half drama and finality As the game moved into the second half, the tension escalated significantly. A flurry of bookings was issued to Julian Contrera , Oscar Cortes , and Juan Bisanz , indicating the growing desperation on the field. The match took a dramatic turn in the 66th minute when Jordy Caicedo was sent off, leaving Huracan to navigate the final portion of the match with ten men. Sarmiento capitalized on the numerical advantage with clinical efficiency. In the 86th minute, Lucas Suarez found the back of the net after a perfectly timed assist from Gaston Gonzalez , effectively putting the result beyond doubt. The final whistle confirmed a deserved victory for the hosts, who maintained their composure in a demanding fixture."
